 even under the plates  they're served on that signature salad  black lung is delivered on a cement  cast of the sidewalk outside his  mother's house in west philadelphia  the display and converse with the notion  of conflict and urban spaces in life  notes from a black pantry has yams  cabbage and carrots  it's a still life it's a representation  of a still life of a photo that i took  of my wife's kitchen  and there's an all black dish called  clorindy named for the 1898 musical by  paul lawrence dunbar and william marion  cook  beef tartar stained black with squid ink  and encased in a rice wafer shell  which represents a glass ceiling meant  to be shattered which one do we eat with  your hands no is it really no the fork  you're messing with yeah the sublime  parker house roll is made with  sweet potatoes inside i'm extremely  influenced  by you can go ahead and say it's  delicious it's fine  it is delicious everyone everyone's like  like going bananas over these but  the bakery department here did such a  great job i was really influenced by  george washington carver and his use of  crops  specifically the sweet potato crop so  this is roasted sweet potato in the  center with butter and the  you know butter makes everything better  yeah it's awesome then  there are the desserts including  honeysuckle ice cream  and a black walnut pound cake with cabin  spiced icing  cow pee coffee and molasses a tribute to  famed american chef edna lewis  the woman who inspired tate and if you  notice that the plate itself  is very different from every other plate  i call these grandma plates because when  i was growing up  like myself and all my friends their  grandmas had the china cabinet  and there were a bunch of plates that  you don't touch unless it's a special  occasion  and so because she's my adopted culinary  grandma i wanted to put it on a very  beautiful plate for her  finally antebellum hudu with ingredients  he read about in a book about healing in  slave communities  sorghum peach jam black walnuts bone  marrow and chickweed  with burnt whiskey which came from a  woman named elsie  and a helping hand from his wife sybil  when you read records of things that  happened  especially during slavery like the  person who was enslaved is not named  especially not a black woman  so for this book to actually have her  name was very important to me  um my wife wrote a children's book  called elsie and so  that reading immediately connected me to  her and so the cup that this burnt  whiskey is in that's a burnt whiskey  tonic for health  is formed and shaped by sybil's hand so  that when the guest is dining  that's this yep yeah you're holding her  hand that's great  she's delivering new health that's great  ted has also created a small book of  remembrances  drawings and writings unlike any menu  we've ever seen  i get the sense that sometimes you have  a tough time getting out of your own  head  yeah yeah that's true and  the poetry helps with that yeah for sure  um it's definitely an outlet i've always  written in creating this concept  uh the poetry became really important  because i knew that if i started plating  dishes like  the black lung dish and said that it was  it represented black culture people  would like well it's a salad like how  does that represent black culture yeah  um and so the poetry emerged as a way  for me to get ahead of having to have a  conversation and justify what i'm doing  20 years from now where do you want to  be what do you want to be doing  uh teaching children how to live  and that means teaching them not just to  cook it means everything  anything anything and you know it's not  just me there's a  nigerian proverb that goes one tree does  not make a forest  right i am not i am not the sole person  or the knower of anything  really all i know is that i have the  capacity  to offer the gift that i've been given  to other people  he put so much thought into everything  he does  his one day dream is to open a community  center and cafe  and meat market and restaurants in west  philadelphia called honeysuckle  provisions  the honeysuckle pop-up was what he did  before that's the long-term  vision when he's done with this but i  have for you guys one of the  one of the best things something that's  become a hit there at stone barns right  now which is this parker house roll  right with the sweet potato stuffed  inside  it is so good they delivered them for us  just um last night we heated them up for  everybody  so anyway they're incredible so how do  you eat and then we'll take a bite  yeah no i was just thinking that after  that meal it didn't look like it was  rather  filling this might fill me up but got  the ice cream we got the kool-aid  we got the beef tartare we've got food  in your mouth

